# Build staging: the assembler, its logs, and the intermediate REL/HEX
# files it produces.  EGT8080.COM itself IS committed (one binary you can
# copy straight to a CP/M drive without owning a toolchain).
build/

# zxcc is copied in from the RomWBW distribution by `make tools`; it is
# third-party GPL software with its own upstream, not part of EGT8080.
#
# Named exactly, not as `tools/`.  The broad form said "third-party" and
# meant it, but `tools/` is also where this project's OWN build scripts
# live - so when the porter and check8080.py arrived they were silently
# untracked, and the 8080 source shipped as a 180 KB generated file with
# no generator and no checker in the repository.  `make` on a fresh clone
# stopped with "No rule to make target 'tools/check8080.py'", and three
# documents promised a safety mechanism that was not there.  An ignore
# rule should exclude what it names.
tools/zxcc-src/
